{
  "_about": "Basements & Basilisks v0.25: every hero number. Read by the test bench (and later the prototype). Behaviour lives in testbench/behaviour.js. Approved changes through 25 Nov are in.",
  "_howToRead": {
    "roll": "A roll is { dice, perTier, bonus, low, high }. dice like \"2d8\" or \"1d4+3\". perTier: the dice count is multiplied by the hero's tier. bonus: an ability score (its modifier is added) or a number. low/high: what changes on a Low or High ability roll, either \"+1\"/\"-1\" dice or a whole new dice string.",
    "byRoll": "{ low, mid, high } gives a value for each ability-roll result. A natural 20 counts as High and doubles the dice.",
    "job": "attack = charges per basic attack; hit = charges when hit (15 per hit); time = charges over time (100 per 5s, faster with INT). Same for everyone in a job.",
    "interval": "Seconds between basic attacks. speedScaling: how strongly attack-speed bonuses shorten it (default 1).",
    "chargeToCast": "Charge needed to cast (default 100). This sets the ability's size: about 60 small, 100 medium, 180 big, 300 nuke (rules.config.json abilitySizes).",
    "benchJob": "Which job benchmark the hero is measured against: frontline, brawler, attacker, caster or support (rules.config.json jobTargets).",
    "size": "Ability size: small, medium, big or nuke. Sets chargeToCast and the value each cast should deliver (rules.config.json abilitySizes).",
    "enabled": "false switches a hero off everywhere (shop, bot, tests) while keeping their numbers.",
    "startCharge": "Charge at the start of a fight; \"full\" means the hero's whole chargeToCast."
  },
